# Cargo build artefacts (per-target subdirectories produced by `cargo build`
# and friends).
/target

# Generated site output (`euv build --out-dir www`).
/www

# `Cargo.lock` is intentionally NOT tracked for this crate.

# `euv-docs` is a single-binary WebAssembly application built and shipped
# from a single workspace root. There is no downstream consumer that would
# need a reproducible Cargo.lock, so the lock file is regenerated on
# every CI build from the Cargo.toml version constraints. This guarantees
# the deploy always picks up the latest matching `euv` / `euv-ui` patch
# release (e.g. `0.18.x`) without requiring a follow-up `cargo update`
# PR every time upstream publishes a fix.
Cargo.lock
